      "meaning": "an enactment is presumed not to apply to facts completed before it came into force, or to interfere with vested rights, unless the Legislature says so expressly or by necessary implication; a repeal does not affect the previous operation of the repealed Act, rights or liabilities that came into existence under it, or offences committed against it; proceedings continue under the new or amended Act, whose procedure applies to matters that happened before; where the new Act provides a lesser penalty, the lesser one applies",
